        // Better: we can modify the test to not rely on Log internals, but assert on something else that diverges.
        // The only observable divergence between the two versions is the behavior of CashOut: reference returns normally after logging, second version reverts on successful call.
        // So we can catch the revert and assert that in reference it does NOT revert, while second version DOES revert.
